warning
# Issue #2434: the pass-end tracker-write flush could not commit the local
# backend's accumulated issue-file writes this pass -- HEAD detached, a
# merge/rebase in progress, a failed commit group, or the writes flushed
# only partially. Warning, not error: nothing is lost (the next pass's
# flush sweeps the dirt up; the flush rescan reads the real working tree),
# and a one-pass deferral heals itself. But repetition means the consumer
# repo's tracker files have stayed dirty across multiple passes -- the
# accumulation the flush exists to prevent -- so ``charlie doctor``'s
# "local tracker writes" check counts these events within a window and
# warns past its threshold. Emitted at most once per loop pass.
